                    insight_genuine:        `Genuine alignment held: the team is behind you for real, the early win landed, and the board's confidence is earned — not performed. The journey can now sustain itself through the harder phases.`,
                    insight_compliance:     `You bought a “yes,” not alignment. The room agrees and the resistance went underground; in six months a stalled execution will tell you the difference between compliance and commitment.`,
                    insight_boardlost:      `The board's two-quarter patience ran out before the strategy was tested. Whatever alignment you built, you lost the clock — and with it the family bloc's backing.`,
                    insight_stalled:        `The transformation stalled: not enough genuine alignment, not enough momentum, and a board no longer sure it backed the right CEO.`,
                    insight_misdiagnosed:   `You misread the Infrastructure President's real driver early — and that one error shaped every move after it. Identity resistance answered with arithmetic never moves.`,
                    insight_capital:        `Touching the SGD 180M before the team was aligned armed the skeptics and confirmed their story. Sequencing isn't a detail — it decided the outcome.`,
                    insight_founder:        `You transformed around the founder instead of with him. He is still the chair your board confidence runs through; the loyalties he commands cost you more than his title suggested.`,
                    insight_talent:         `The two cloud leaders walked. You can't run a cloud-and-AI transformation after its engine leaves — momentum never recovered.`,
                    insight_risk:           `Derailment risk stayed high throughout: a visible fracture and talent flight were always one wrong move away. You were managing a transformation on the edge of breaking.`,

                    hint_diagnose:          `Re-read the Infrastructure President. If you're treating his resistance as a business-case problem, you're solving the wrong problem — and every later move inherits the error.`,
                    hint_compliance:        `You're accumulating compliance, not alignment. Pressure and removal buy a “yes” that goes underground. Build it WITH the team, not against them.`,
                    hint_capital:           `Moving the capital before alignment armed the skeptics. Slow down on the SGD 180M and rebuild the team behind you first.`,
